A write, from the wire to the row
A client sends a resource to the tenant's own FHIR face. The face parses the
bytes once and hands them to the object engine with the type the tenant
declared. The engine derives the searchable envelope from the payload and
resolves the record's identity, then writes the payload, the envelope, the
trail entry and the change event to the tenant's database in one transaction.
The version comes back and the face answers the client with a status, an ETag
and a Location.
